        "original_id": "430ebfc0-6cd6-5cfe-98c4-77f636e17420",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Lorde\n- Songs: \"Tennis Court\", \"Royals\", \"Mother Mother\"\n- Albums and EPs: \"Pure Heroine\", \"The Love Club EP\"\n- Companies: Universal Music Group\n- Charts: Billboard Alternative Songs\n\nFacts:\n- In 2012, Lorde released \"Royals\" on her debut extended play, \"The Love Club EP\".\n- On 7 June 2013, Universal Music Group released \"Tennis Court\" as the second single from \"Pure Heroine\", following \"Royals\".\n- In 2013, Lorde later included \"Royals\" on her debut studio album, \"Pure Heroine\".\n- In August 2013, \"Royals\" by Lorde became the first song by a female solo artist to top the renamed Billboard Alternative Songs chart since \"Mother Mother\" had last done so before the chart's renaming.",
